/comments/4064127144","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115331#issuecomment-4064127144","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115331","id":4064127144,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7yPaio","user":{"login":"BinaryGleam","id":42295409,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMjk1NDA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42295409?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BinaryGleam","html_url":"https://github.com/BinaryGleam","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BinaryGleam/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BinaryGleam/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BinaryGleam/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BinaryGleam/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BinaryGleam/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BinaryGleam/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BinaryGleam/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BinaryGleam/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BinaryGleam/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-15T23:08:13Z","updated_at":"2026-03-15T23:08:13Z","body":"> Hello, I have exactly the same problem. After exporting for web and playing an AudioPlayer2D, the game freezes for a while. Have you found any solution?\n\nHeym sorry for the late reply. Basically I just play all the sounds of a scene at the start of a scene so it freezes for less time ^^' Sorry, its more of a work around than an actual solution","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4064127144/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4067068780","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115331#issuecomment-4067068780","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115331","id":4067068780,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7yaots","user":{"login":"lukepass","id":6429961,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0Mjk5NjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6429961?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepass","html_url":"https://github.com/lukepass","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepass/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepass/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepass/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepass/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepass/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lukepass/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-16T11:44:15Z","updated_at":"2026-03-16T11:44:15Z","body":"That's exactly what I did for now. I'm starting the audio at zero volume and then I just `seek` it to `0.0` when it's needed.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4067068780/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4068656380","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115331#issuecomment-4068656380","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115331","id":4068656380,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ygsT8","user":{"login":"BinaryGleam","id":42295409,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMjk1NDA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42295409?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BinaryGleam","html_url":"https://github.com/BinaryGleam","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BinaryGleam/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BinaryGleam/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BinaryGleam/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BinaryGleam/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BinaryGleam/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BinaryGleam/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BinaryGleam/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BinaryGleam/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BinaryGleam/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-16T15:46:52Z","updated_at":"2026-03-16T15:46:52Z","body":"> That's exactly what I did for now. I'm starting the audio at zero volume and then I just `seek` it to `0.0` when it's needed.\n\nIt saddens me to hear that my friend. I really hope a solution will eventually come because it bloats any web project to do so","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4068656380/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5897454039","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115331#issuecomment-5897454039","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115331","id":5897454039,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABX4QB1w","user":{"login":"Faless","id":1687918,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2ODc5MTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1687918?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless","html_url":"https://github.com/Faless","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-29T19:47:18Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T19:47:18Z","body":"The problem is that web exports now uses `Sample` play mode by default.\nThis is good for sound effects and can work very well on non-threaded builds even on low-end devices, but is not great for longer compressed streams as it forces them to be mixed all at once on load.\n\nYou can try setting the audio player to use `Stream` mode:\n\n<img width=\"282\" height=\"419\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/80ccea94-30eb-4679-8442-f06ab19412b2\" />\n\nOr change the default in the project settings:\n\n<img width=\"1182\" height=\"721\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4da4166c-f231-411a-bdbd-b7a378623f50\" />\n\nBut to minimize the risk of crackling audio with `Stream` mode you'll have to export with threads.\n\n<img width=\"882\" height=\"419\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/83476571-b476-427a-90cf-dc6e32cdc83e\" />","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5897454039/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]